1. THIRD-PARTY DATA UNDER `data/anchors/`
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The 0BSD grant above covers this project's own code, documentation and
configuration. It cannot and does not relicense third-party material vendored
under `data/anchors/`, which stays under its originators' terms. Sources and
checksums are catalogued in `data/anchors/MANIFEST.md`:

  - OpenStreetMap extracts (`*_places.geojson`, `*_roads.geojson`,
    `osm_*_raw.json`) — (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database Licence
    (ODbL) v1.0. Note that the ODbL is a share-alike licence: if you distribute
    a derived database you have obligations under it that this file does not
    lift.
  - Census and municipal tables — data.opencity.in and the Pune Municipal
    Corporation, published as open data.
  - A GTFS extract obtained from a third-party repository.
  - `gadgil_poona_survey_part1.pdf` — D. R. Gadgil, "Poona: A Socio-Economic
    Survey, Part I — Economic", a scan from the Internet Archive's Digital
    Library of India collection.

If you only take the code, none of this concerns you. If you redistribute the
repository or the data, check those terms yourself.


2. EVERY PERSON IN THIS SIMULATION IS INVENTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project simulates a real place — four peths of Pune's old city, with real
street geometry and real building and business names taken from OpenStreetMap.
The people are not real. Every household, name, age, occupation, religion,
income, illness, argument, rumour and misfortune is synthesised from a seed and
a census marginal, or written by a language model. Any resemblance to a living
person is coincidence produced by a random number generator.

Nothing this software outputs is a statement of fact about any real person,
family, community, business, institution or public body, including those whose
names appear in the map data. Model-generated text may be wrong, offensive, or
defamatory-sounding about real named places; it is fiction generated by
machine and is not an assertion by the author or by anyone else.

If you publish or act on anything this software produces, that is your decision
and your responsibility.


3. IT CALLS PAID APIS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Running this with scenes enabled sends requests to third-party language-model
providers using your own API key and spends your own money. You are responsible
for your keys, your spend, and your compliance with those providers' terms. The
author is not.
